  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reconciliation and Peace-Building Actions in Bogot&#xE1; D.C.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support reparation and peace-building processes promoted in Bogota, D.C., for the restoration of trust and the peaceful resolution of conflicts by applying tested methodologies by the current local administration through 6 components: i)Local integration: implement psychosocial methodologies to advance the comprehensive reparation of forced displacement victims. ii)Training and pedagogy for peace: Training programs for peace, reconciliation, and non-repetition. One rural program in Sumapaz and one urban program in Bosa and Ciudad Bolivar. iii)Memory: Develop memory exercises and social appropriation of public spaces actions through participatory methodologies, considering the impacts of the armed conflict in Sumapaz. iv)Non-stigmatization and reconciliation: Develop community and cultural actions aimed at the non-stigmatization of former FARC-EP members and ex-combatants in Bogot&#xE1;, D.C. v)Restorative justice and search for persons: Restorative justice actions through the TOAR Route, psychosocial and legal accompaniment to victims in the Comprehensive Peace System, and processes to strengthen the search for disappeared persons. vi) Dissemination: Implement a communications plan to socialize the actions to guarantee victims&#xB4; rights that are promoted by the local government in Bogot&#xE1;</narrative>
  </description>
